course: dictionary
lesson: 357
title: Antecedent: the word that comes before
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: An antecedent is the noun that came before a pronoun and that the pronoun points back to. Pronouns like he, she, it, they and his are short words that stand in for a noun. «Sam lost his hat.» Ask yourself: whose hat? The answer is Sam, so Sam is the antecedent of his.
explain: A pronoun needs a clear antecedent. If it could point to more than one noun, the sentence is unclear. «Ella told Mia that she had won.» Who had won, Ella or Mia? Read the sentence again and decide which noun she points back to, then say why.
explain: Antecedent has other meanings too. Your antecedents are your ancestors, the family who came before you. In history, the antecedents of a war are the events that led to it. In every case, an antecedent comes earlier and leads to what follows.
fact: An antecedent is the noun or phrase that a pronoun refers back to.
fact: In «Sam lost his hat», Sam is the antecedent of his.
fact: A pronoun is ambiguous when it could point back to more than one noun.
fact: As a plural noun, antecedents means your ancestors or family background.
fact: As a formal adjective, antecedent means coming before.
exercise: «Sam lost his hat.» What is the antecedent of his? | Hat | *Sam | Lost
exercise: What does antecedent mean in grammar? | A word that comes after a pronoun | A kind of question | A type of verb | *The noun or phrase a pronoun refers back to
exercise: In «Ella told Mia that she had won», why is she unclear? | *It could point back to Ella or to Mia | She is always plural | There is no noun in the sentence | It is a verb
test: In «The dog chased the cat until it ran up a tree», what is the antecedent of it? | Chased | *The cat | A tree | The dog
test: Which word means coming before? | Ancient | Future | *Antecedent | Final
exam: «The bird left its nest when the storm came.» What is the antecedent of its? | Storm | Nest | *The bird
